            <div xml:id="d899">

                <pb facs="0936" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg824"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 891.001.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Persian
                    Chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your announcement of the death of His Imperial Highness the Regent has been
                    received by me with great regret. Accept an expression of my sympathy.</p>
                <p>The President has by telegraph conveyed his condolence to His Imperial Majesty
                    the Shah, and the Secretary of State has also telegraphed in the same sense to
                    the minister of foreign affairs of Persia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
